Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 21:01:01 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1162/1252] HERESY 1167: the third towel: Clear asks, the
 music's lengths in time, guards that say why, Play new takes, the column's
 star
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Viktor's third towel of 05.10.2026, and what he added to it the same evening:
· Clear asks first (a slip no longer empties the form); Plan score only is off in Direct (it writes no score); Save
  and the guide live in ☰; the fifth tab says Trainer; the Creator's four drawers one under another, each the
  column's width; the workspace in hand reads in the rooms' colour in the dark themes, every dropdown's list in its
  theme's colours.
· The music's Min and Max length in time (25 tokens a second): Max follows Max length (the engine caps there
  anyway), Min in seconds behind its lock; the score's stay in tokens. A prompt that capped the music lower than its
  Max length gets that as its Max length. The music's bounds reach 16:00 (Direct gives it nearly the whole window).
· Guards on Guidance (1–4: Viktor's word, the engine itself sets none), ODE steps, Max length, variations and peak
  clip, and every knob's guard says why in a line of its own; Guidance from 2.6 is said to be an experiment; a field
  emptied shows its default again when you leave it, not at the keystroke that emptied it (Backspace in Guidance).
· The texts as the defaults are now: the Style slider (1.2–2.0, every position two passes), Guidance (Viktor's
  measure: 1.4–1.6 stable, 2.0 dynamic, 2.4 the edge, from 2.6 the music cut short), the floors (200 and 0:30), the
  music's ceiling, Max length; the built-in profiles' floors too (750 and 200, not the release's 200 and 32).
· The meter: Direct writes no score, so the score's budget no longer turns a reading red; over the window in Direct
  it says how long the sound beside the text can be.
· Play new takes, the player's third switch: a song made here plays when it is done unless something plays.
· The rooms' column: the star beside the thumbs; a refused rating is said, not swallowed; a catalog asked before a
  rating and answered after it no longer takes the rating back.
· The artwork: Download in its overlay (the browser's menu is off); on the Librarian's tiles it is the card's right
  side, its whole height.
· The Writer: its one button filled, on the right, «Send the request to LLM», what is happening on its left;
  Ctrl+Enter in the brief; its requests and answers (with their tokens) in the server log.
· 38 words in the seven languages.

cdp-console 334/0/7, check-i18n 14/0, check-player 3/0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
